{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"a8153a6b9d696e0fa75f9872bf702a7e4bbd08729621ade38e74c1f1d4829836","digest":{"component_or_area":"CompletionAgentStep recovery handler","key_entities":["CompletionAgentStep._recover","src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_recovery.py","show_ticket","_reads.show_ticket","failure_diagnostic","RebarError","LLMError","LLMBudgetExhaustedError","CompletionRecoveryError","raise_completion_workflow_failure","stage=preflight"],"problem_keywords":["completion recovery","prelude failure","diagnostic loss","error handling","LLMBudgetExhaustedError"],"propositions":["The prelude show_ticket call in CompletionAgentStep._recover executes outside the try block that builds failure_diagnostic, causing RebarError to escape without diagnostic context.","When show_ticket raises RebarError, the primary run's aggregate_* repetition and budget diagnostic keys are lost because failure_diagnostic remains None.","The gate-error sidecar is not emitted when RebarError from show_ticket occurs during recovery.","Moving show_ticket inside the existing try block will ensure preflight RebarError failures are caught and produce CompletionRecoveryError with preserved primary diagnostic.","The existing recovery-failure and happy-path behaviors must remain unchanged after moving the prelude into the try block."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787618862128719396,"uuid":"a301f115-24df-456f-9901-888b2ca57a55"}